Derived work includes:
  - The screen-capture and OCR approach (mss + pytesseract), and the measured
    preprocessing decision not to upscale.
  - The tuning defaults for the three capture regions (CAPTURE_REGION,
    TEAM_ICON_REGION, SCORE_REGION) and MONITOR_INDEX.
  - Faction detection by circular-mean hue sampling of the HUD icon.
  - Scoreboard reading, including the "exactly three digits or discard the
    whole read" strictness.
  - The text parsing expressions for the pause-menu server panel, the queue
    bar (with its countdown deliberately excluded), and the menu/splash
    not-in-game detection.
  - The debounce rule (a reading must occur twice in a row), the heartbeat,
    the score-update throttle, and the server/team-independent tracking.
  - The tray-icon approach and the region-preview drag-to-set interaction.

Changes made in this project, which are NOT from the upstream original:
  - Transport moved from a Discord bot token to an incoming webhook, including
    per-execution username/avatar_url identity, message re-creation on identity
    change, and recovery when a stored message id is gone.
  - A first-run setup wizard replacing manual .env and region_preview.py steps.
  - Configuration and state stored in %APPDATA% rather than beside the script.
  - Bundled Tesseract resolution, so no system install is required.
  - One bug fix in the region-matching expression: upstream's REGION_RE
    matched the queue countdown's parentheses and could read "(0:42)" as a
    region name.

